<title>USA: Farmer Mac settles suit with Western Farm.</title>
<headline>Farmer Mac settles suit with Western Farm.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Agricultural Mortgage Corp said on Friday it settled the lawsuit it brought against its one-time strategic-alliance partner, Western Farm Credit Bank, terminating the alliance without any adverse effect on Farmer Mac's finances.</p>
<p>Farmer Mac waived all restrictions on Western's ability to sell 63,000 Farmer Mac shares of Class C non-voting stock, which were sold to Western under the now-abandoned strategic alliance agreement.  Farmer Mac also reacquired 93,000 shares of its Class B voting stock that had been sold to Western Farm.</p>
</text>
